1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 7: simple HF beams - Moxon and 2-element Yagi

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:14,072
YA-NEC course, lesson 7: a simple HF beam from the calculators - the Moxon and the 2-element Yagi.

3
00:00:14,122 --> 00:00:23,072
Moxon rectangle (Les Moxon G6XN; dimensions from L.B. Cebik's MOXGEN, as used by DK7ZB). Frequency 14.15 MHz, 2 mm wire.

4
00:00:23,122 --> 00:00:32,405
A 7.72 m, B 1.18 m, C 0.20 m, D 1.44 m. In free space: SWR 1.01, 6.02 dBi and F/B 41 dB - a deep rear null with two elements.

5
00:00:32,455 --> 00:00:41,189
Now 12 m above average ground.

6
00:00:41,239 --> 00:00:47,723
SWR 1.09, 11.08 dBi with the ground reflection, maximum at 24 degrees; F/B 18.5 dB.

7
00:00:47,773 --> 00:00:58,796
'Create the NEC model and check it'.

8
00:00:58,846 --> 00:01:04,529
58 + j0.1 ohm, SWR 1.16 on 50 ohm: the Moxon is fed directly with coax.

9
00:01:04,579 --> 00:01:18,788
Now a 2-element Yagi with the Multiband Yagi calculator, 20 m only.

10
00:01:18,838 --> 00:01:28,327
One driven dipole and one parasitic element per band; we keep only 20 m.

11
00:01:28,377 --> 00:01:37,389
Average ground at 10 m, then 'Tune and verify' - reflector-dipole.

12
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:43,551
Reflector 10.64 m at 4.32 m: SWR 1.03 at band centre, 12.2 dBi, F/B 13.6 dB.

13
00:01:43,601 --> 00:01:55,680
Same thing with a director: dipole-director.

14
00:01:55,730 --> 00:02:01,825
Director 9.19 m at 1.96 m: 10.6 dBi, F/B only 4.8 dB, impedance 39 ohm.

15
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:11,628
Reflector or director: the Moxon wins on F/B, the reflector Yagi on gain. The 3-element Yagi comes in lesson 15, with the Optimizer.

16
00:02:11,678 --> 00:02:17,628
Moxon and 2-element Yagi: two beams in a few clicks. Next lesson: HF beams with traps and ground. 73 de IC8TEM
